    {
      "beat_id": "B01",
      "estimated_duration_s": 12,
      "narration_text": "This is Liam, in for Bear. Entanglement is not merely yes or no. For a pure pair of qubits, the entropy of either subsystem gives an amount: zero for a product state, one ebit for a Bell pair.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "CARD",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "type",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeComposerAsk",
          "props": {
            "command": "Measure how much entanglement a pure two-qubit state contains.",
            "topic": "QUANTUM MECHANICS — ENTANGLEMENT",
            "segment": "The Entropy Thermometer",
            "greeting": "Salaam, Liam",
            "runningText": "turning Schmidt weights into ebits…",
            "output": [
              "Product pure state: 0 ebits.",
              "Maximally entangled qubit pair: 1 ebit."
            ],
            "folderLabel": "@NikBearBrown",
            "modelLabel": "Claude",
            "effortLabel": "High"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B01.mp4",
            "at": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B01.mp3",
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B01.mp4",
        "filled_by": "media",
        "at": "2026-07-18T23:40:55"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B02",
      "estimated_duration_s": 11,
      "narration_text": "Consider cosine theta zero-zero plus sine theta one-one, with theta between zero and pi over four. These are already Schmidt-form amplitudes.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "scan"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B02.mp3",
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B02.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T23:40:55"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B03",
      "estimated_duration_s": 11,
      "narration_text": "The subsystem probabilities are cosine squared theta and sine squared theta. Entanglement entropy is the binary entropy of those two probabilities, measured with base-two logarithms.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "accumulate"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B03.mp3",
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B03.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T23:40:55"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B04",
      "estimated_duration_s": 10,
      "narration_text": "At theta zero, all weight sits on zero-zero. The state factors, either subsystem is pure, and the entanglement entropy is zero.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "threshold"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B04.mp3",
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B04.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T23:40:55"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B05",
      "estimated_duration_s": 11,
      "narration_text": "At theta pi over four, the weights are equal halves. The state is a Bell pair and the subsystem entropy reaches one ebit, the maximum for two qubits.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "transform"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B05.mp3",
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B05.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T23:40:55"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B06",
      "estimated_duration_s": 12,
      "narration_text": "For root three over two times zero-zero plus one half times one-one, the probabilities are three quarters and one quarter. Their binary entropy is about zero point eight one one ebits.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "compare"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B06.mp3",
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B06.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T23:40:55"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B07",
      "estimated_duration_s": 11,
      "narration_text": "The state is entangled because both Schmidt terms are present, but less than maximal because the weights are unequal. More balanced local uncertainty means more pure-state bipartite entanglement.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "compare"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B07.mp3",
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B07.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T23:40:55"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B08",
      "estimated_duration_s": 12,
      "narration_text": "For many identical copies of a known bipartite pure state, this entropy also sets an asymptotic conversion rate under ideal local operations and classical communication. It is not a one-shot guarantee for a finite batch.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "threshold"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B08.mp3",
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B08.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T23:40:55"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B09",
      "estimated_duration_s": 11,
      "narration_text": "And the simple entropy rule has a boundary: it is the standard entanglement measure for bipartite pure states. Mixed and multipartite states require more care and can have inequivalent measures.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "collapse"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B09.mp3",
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B09.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T23:40:55"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B10",
      "estimated_duration_s": 13,
      "narration_text": "Your turn. The Schmidt probabilities are three quarters and one quarter. Is the state separable, maximally entangled, or in between? Pause before the answer: in between, with about zero point eight one one ebits.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "CARD",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "type",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeComposerAsk",
          "props": {
            "command": "Your turn: classify Schmidt probabilities 3/4 and 1/4.",
            "topic": "QUANTUM MECHANICS — CHECK",
            "segment": "Read the Thermometer",
            "greeting": "Over to you, Liam",
            "runningText": "waiting for the entropy classification…",
            "output": [
              "Both weights nonzero: entangled.",
              "Unequal weights: 0.811 ebits, below the 1-ebit maximum."
            ],
            "folderLabel": "@NikBearBrown",
            "modelLabel": "Claude",
            "effortLabel": "High"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B10.mp4",
            "at": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B10.mp3",
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B10.mp4",
        "filled_by": "media",
        "at": "2026-07-18T23:40:55"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B11",
      "estimated_duration_s": 8,
      "narration_text": "Entanglement has a thermometer: the entropy of either half of a bipartite pure state, read in ebits.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "fade"
      },
